WEBVTT

00:01.390 --> 00:03.730
I want to be happy.

00:24.830 --> 00:27.630
I want to be happy.

00:29.750 --> 00:31.460
I wanted to be happy since I was little.

00:35.130 --> 00:36.390
I wanted to be happy.

00:41.220 --> 00:42.980
Anyone would want to be happy.

00:45.480 --> 00:46.690
But...

00:46.850 --> 00:49.400
How do you become happy?

00:52.400 --> 00:54.490
I want to be happy.

01:01.450 --> 01:04.120
I want to be happy...

01:08.130 --> 01:12.050
Senpachi Fansubs presents

01:08.130 --> 01:12.050
Denpa Teki na Kanojo

01:12.800 --> 01:14.880
Game of Happiness

01:15.060 --> 01:17.430
You pervert!

01:16.680 --> 01:17.930
- I didn't do it!

01:17.950 --> 01:18.500
What!?

01:18.540 --> 01:19.610
You did it!

01:19.630 --> 01:21.620
You were touching me on the train!

01:21.920 --> 01:23.400
How disgraceful!

01:23.400 --> 01:26.200
Don't waste time with the criminal, just call the police.

01:26.360 --> 01:27.270
What happened here?

01:27.530 --> 01:30.070
This person here tried to touch me on the train.

01:30.210 --> 01:32.270
He must have done this before.

01:32.390 --> 01:33.670
Please arrest him.

01:33.750 --> 01:36.180
Yeah, a person like him should die.

01:36.380 --> 01:37.360
Understood.

01:37.780 --> 01:40.190
Then... you, can you come with me?

01:40.420 --> 01:41.850
I will call the police.

01:41.920 --> 01:44.080
I didn't do it!

01:44.650 --> 01:46.760
I will never let you run away!

01:47.180 --> 01:48.050
You bastard!

01:48.150 --> 01:49.110
Please wait a minute!

01:49.170 --> 01:51.070
He didn't do it!

01:51.250 --> 01:52.590
Who are you?

01:52.650 --> 01:53.500
Go away!

01:53.580 --> 01:55.050
It's got nothing to do with you!

01:55.080 --> 01:56.380
It is...

01:58.320 --> 01:59.340
something to do with me.

01:59.420 --> 02:01.100
I am his girlfriend!

02:01.480 --> 02:02.450
Hey, Hikaru.

02:03.020 --> 02:04.440
So what!?

02:04.440 --> 02:06.610
He won't be touching you because...

02:07.010 --> 02:10.010
... because I always make him satisfied sexually!

02:14.290 --> 02:15.620
Okay, let's go.

02:15.970 --> 02:17.690
Are you kidding me?

02:17.950 --> 02:19.240
And isn't it strange?

02:19.280 --> 02:21.740
You just pop up from nowhere and say you're his girlfriend!

02:21.900 --> 02:23.970
Don't lie to me!

02:35.010 --> 02:37.310
Thanks for helping me, Hikaru.

02:38.590 --> 02:40.080
If you didn't help me,

02:40.310 --> 02:42.170
I would have either been caught or have had to make trouble.

02:43.150 --> 02:46.280
Either way I'd have gotten arrested.

02:46.400 --> 02:47.530
Everything...!

02:48.180 --> 02:50.070
Everything is ruined!

02:51.070 --> 02:54.220
I can't believe I gave my first kiss to someone like this!

02:54.250 --> 02:56.810
Everything is ruined!

03:00.950 --> 03:04.810
What? Why did you do something this embarrassing anyway?

03:04.830 --> 03:06.370
You pervert!

03:06.510 --> 03:08.560
When will you stop playing with women?

03:08.770 --> 03:12.230
You always do what you want.

03:12.310 --> 03:13.910
Why are you so thick-skinned?

03:13.970 --> 03:15.350
You also...

03:15.350 --> 03:16.240
You did everything wrong!

03:16.250 --> 03:17.860
Okay, I am sorry. It's all my fault.

03:18.100 --> 03:21.610
Yeah, everything! Everything is your fault!

03:24.150 --> 03:25.210
Forget it.

03:26.550 --> 03:28.660
Forget everything that happened today.

03:28.780 --> 03:30.830
Don't tell anyone!

03:31.110 --> 03:34.000
It is our secret.

03:34.690 --> 03:36.260
If it is a secret, how will I forget it?

03:36.860 --> 03:37.400
Sorry...

03:38.260 --> 03:40.140
What's wrong, Lord Juu?

03:44.500 --> 03:46.010
Did Hikaru make that?

03:48.670 --> 03:49.290
Yes.

03:50.670 --> 03:52.040
Is she okay?

03:52.170 --> 03:52.700
Yes.

03:53.300 --> 03:55.750
Is there anything between you two?

03:58.420 --> 03:59.020
Nothing.

04:00.860 --> 04:03.180
She likes you very much.

04:04.070 --> 04:04.890
So...

04:07.860 --> 04:09.780
Hikaru is a good sister.

04:10.700 --> 04:13.140
She loves me

04:13.540 --> 04:15.420
and I love her, too.

04:17.160 --> 04:22.090
If it's possible, I would like to make her something to eat.

04:23.680 --> 04:28.890
But every time I try to make something, I am always stopped by my mum and Hikaru.

04:33.740 --> 04:35.430
You love her.

04:37.030 --> 04:39.500
Hey Ame, what is love?

04:40.250 --> 04:42.330
It is the first letter in the Japanese alphabet.

04:45.120 --> 04:46.260
Sorry for making a joke.

04:46.620 --> 04:49.720
- Juuzawa Juu of second year class 13...

04:50.330 --> 04:53.220
- Juuzawa Juu of second year class 13...

04:54.150 --> 04:56.410
- Please come to the Student Council.

04:57.720 --> 05:00.350
I only called for Juuzawa.

05:00.760 --> 05:02.590
Can you please leave?

05:02.890 --> 05:04.330
Sorry but I can't leave.

05:05.160 --> 05:09.090
Lord Juu and I are connected by strong bonds from our previous lives.

05:09.550 --> 05:14.190
It's something that even Excalibur can't break, Ms. Ayase.

05:16.690 --> 05:18.110
Just ignore her.

05:24.700 --> 05:26.280
I am Ayase Ichiko.

05:27.260 --> 05:32.100
The Vice-President of the Student Council President; I am in the same class as Ochibana.

05:33.190 --> 05:35.580
Do you know the reason why I called you here?

05:36.110 --> 05:36.860
I don't.

05:37.250 --> 05:40.540
My, everyone knows about it.

05:40.940 --> 05:43.130
Do you know, Ochibana?

05:43.890 --> 05:49.060
Juuzawa was accused of molestation.

05:49.900 --> 05:50.590
Molestation?

05:51.230 --> 05:58.250
He even told his lover to kiss him in public to get away with it.

05:59.820 --> 06:00.740
Lover?

06:01.970 --> 06:03.970
I didn't do it!

06:04.130 --> 06:06.800
Do you have any proof?

06:07.180 --> 06:08.070
That's...

06:08.460 --> 06:10.280
Lord Juu wouldn't have done it.

06:11.340 --> 06:12.950
Why do you trust him so much?

06:13.660 --> 06:15.470
Because Juuzawa is Lord Juu.

06:15.990 --> 06:17.700
That's enough of a reason.

06:21.450 --> 06:24.150
This is surprising, Juuzawa.

06:24.830 --> 06:27.800
I can see that the girl yesterday is not the only girlfriend you've got.

06:27.960 --> 06:28.730
Why you...

06:28.770 --> 06:29.970
What a player!

06:30.420 --> 06:34.420
I just remembered you were a good friend of Satsuki Miya.

06:34.950 --> 06:37.850
You like that type of girl?

06:38.230 --> 06:38.780
I'm going.

06:38.850 --> 06:40.540
Don't leave without me telling you to.

06:46.590 --> 06:51.040
That's not good, you just hit someone in the Student Council.

06:51.090 --> 06:51.760
Wait...

06:53.910 --> 06:57.020
That was your fault, Ayase.

06:57.530 --> 06:58.830
Shiraishi...

06:59.030 --> 06:59.920
Student Council President!

07:00.520 --> 07:03.270
Yes, I am Shiraishi Kaori.

07:03.830 --> 07:05.830
I am sorry that you were insulted.

07:07.020 --> 07:07.790
Ayase.

07:08.780 --> 07:12.420
Juuzawa is here because there wasn't enough to prove anything.

07:13.510 --> 07:17.850
You are in the Student Council. You can't believe everything.

07:20.550 --> 07:20.970
Okay.

07:22.220 --> 07:24.690
I understand why you are annoyed, Juuzawa.

07:25.160 --> 07:26.780
But you cannot be violent.

07:27.330 --> 07:29.240
Can you apologize to Ayase?

07:35.230 --> 07:36.020
Sorry.

07:36.200 --> 07:36.580
Okay.

07:37.060 --> 07:40.880
It's done now.

07:41.680 --> 07:44.080
My deepest apologies, Lord Juu.

07:44.710 --> 07:46.820
I didn't help you when it happened.

07:47.390 --> 07:49.100
Don't worry about it.

07:49.820 --> 07:50.900
It was my fault.

07:51.660 --> 07:54.450
I was saved by the president.

07:54.970 --> 07:56.670
Shiraishi?

07:57.590 --> 08:01.980
She is trusted by the students and the teachers.

08:03.530 --> 08:04.760
There is always someone like her...

08:05.390 --> 08:11.740
But now I know why my class dislikes me.

08:12.690 --> 08:13.200
What's wrong?

08:14.790 --> 08:16.140
Umm, Lord Juu.

08:16.960 --> 08:19.460
Can I ask you a question?

08:19.800 --> 08:20.270
What?

08:20.690 --> 08:23.860
Who is the girlfriend Ayase was talking about?

08:25.360 --> 08:27.170
Eh... that's...

08:29.960 --> 08:30.770
Sorry.

08:31.120 --> 08:32.740
I asked too much.

08:33.200 --> 08:36.080
I don't mind whoever Lord Juu goes out with.

08:41.530 --> 08:44.280
Sorry, let's go.

08:45.980 --> 08:46.280
Okay.

08:51.330 --> 08:52.140
Juuzawa speaking.

08:55.000 --> 08:56.800
Hello? This is Juuzawa speaking.

09:00.850 --> 09:02.000
Did he get the wrong number?

09:05.500 --> 09:06.170
Hello.

09:13.170 --> 09:15.730
Lord Juu, it's about the rumor.

09:15.980 --> 09:17.510
Do you need any help?

09:18.940 --> 09:22.080
The rumor will be gone in a while.

09:22.950 --> 09:23.660
But...

09:24.090 --> 09:25.730
I don't have a good feeling...

09:26.330 --> 09:32.670
Do you know that something strange is happening in the school, Lord Juu?

09:33.070 --> 09:34.160
Something strange?

09:35.150 --> 09:37.460
Simply said, it is basically harassment.

09:38.230 --> 09:41.330
Like... putting pins in a shoe.

09:43.140 --> 09:47.160
Messing up your drawer.

09:47.860 --> 09:49.540
Hiding clothes.

09:50.130 --> 09:50.610
However...

09:51.120 --> 09:55.020
The police doesn't take such things seriously...

09:55.560 --> 09:58.890
but it annoys the person it happens to.

10:00.490 --> 10:05.940
And the rumor is that you are one who's doing it.

10:08.390 --> 10:10.120
Maybe you're thinking too much about it...

10:11.140 --> 10:13.000
I may be thinking too much.

10:13.750 --> 10:15.780
Maybe there aren't enough rumors to prove...

10:16.990 --> 10:21.160
If Lord Juu allows me, I will look into it.

10:21.310 --> 10:22.280
What will you do?

10:22.550 --> 10:23.690
Stop and destroy that person.

10:23.750 --> 10:24.550
Don't do that!

10:25.110 --> 10:27.500
Even if it is, it...

10:28.000 --> 10:29.590
It is better to leave it.

10:29.990 --> 10:30.550
But...

10:31.630 --> 10:33.520
I don't want to get into any trouble any more.

10:36.400 --> 10:37.080
Damn.

10:37.380 --> 10:38.800
Who is doing these annoying things...

10:42.090 --> 10:42.610
Hikaru?

10:46.270 --> 10:46.730
Hey!

10:48.290 --> 10:48.840
What?

10:59.010 --> 11:00.410
I feel sorry.

11:01.530 --> 11:02.810
Wa... wait!

11:03.000 --> 11:04.080
What are you doing?

11:04.260 --> 11:06.060
If I wear clothes I can't do it.

11:06.180 --> 11:06.780
What?

11:06.990 --> 11:07.690
Sex.

11:11.160 --> 11:15.000
It is my first time, but go ahead, do as you like.

11:16.380 --> 11:19.120
Do I need to take my underwear off?

11:21.060 --> 11:22.940
I refuse to do it with you.

11:23.690 --> 11:24.430
Why?

11:24.660 --> 11:26.980
You do it all the time anyway.

11:27.120 --> 11:29.420
Sorry, but I have the right to choose.

11:29.950 --> 11:31.480
I can't do it with you.

11:33.980 --> 11:36.430
It must be... because I am not attractive.

11:38.170 --> 11:40.690
It's not because of that.

11:52.120 --> 11:54.590
I... got dumped.

11:55.630 --> 11:57.150
He is called Ibuki.

11:57.680 --> 11:59.910
I met him in a karate competition.

12:00.690 --> 12:01.910
He is very strong...

12:03.070 --> 12:03.870
and kind...

12:04.990 --> 12:05.960
and I...

12:08.820 --> 12:11.890
but when I said I fancied him...

12:12.630 --> 12:14.660
He looked at me with a horrible look.

12:15.580 --> 12:18.560
I asked him why he was angry.

12:19.480 --> 12:19.960
Then?

12:21.780 --> 12:24.370
He knew...

12:25.880 --> 12:29.350
He knew I kissed you.

12:31.560 --> 12:32.720
Who took this?

12:32.970 --> 12:33.820
I don't know.

12:34.380 --> 12:37.570
It was sent to him.

12:39.710 --> 12:40.730
Can I have this?

12:43.130 --> 12:43.900
What are you going to do with it?

12:44.210 --> 12:45.630
Are, are you going to use it for...

12:45.670 --> 12:46.370
It's not what you think.

12:49.900 --> 12:53.000
If you ask, I wouldn't mind.

12:54.890 --> 12:55.950
Listen to this, Hikaru.

12:57.000 --> 12:59.290
There is no need to find me.

13:00.630 --> 13:01.800
You are definitely cute enough.

13:08.390 --> 13:10.310
This is new, Juuzawa.

13:12.490 --> 13:13.680
The brake on your bike?

13:14.550 --> 13:18.080
Isn't it the harassment around here?

13:19.770 --> 13:20.860
I don't know...

13:21.480 --> 13:23.910
It is strange that it suddenly stopped working...

13:24.700 --> 13:27.720
but I wouldn't blame anyone. Maybe just thinking too much?

13:28.660 --> 13:29.770
Maybe, but...

13:30.420 --> 13:32.000
You should think more sometimes.

13:33.360 --> 13:34.540
You are the Student Council President.

13:35.210 --> 13:36.480
You should know some stuff.

13:38.380 --> 13:41.510
Don't you think... it's happening a lot?

13:46.290 --> 13:46.900
Yes.

13:47.640 --> 13:51.310
The Student Council is busy because of it...

13:53.370 --> 13:57.060
But the teachers... and Satsuki.

13:58.050 --> 14:00.250
They say not to make a big deal out of it.

14:01.340 --> 14:03.330
It seems tiring to be president of the Student Council...

14:05.890 --> 14:07.620
But it's fine.

14:08.710 --> 14:10.490
This could be my punishment.

14:11.060 --> 14:11.500
Punishment?

14:12.620 --> 14:16.850
I... have killed someone before...

14:17.720 --> 14:18.050
What?

14:18.900 --> 14:22.760
It was at secondary school; there was someone who really liked me...

14:24.000 --> 14:26.410
But I was going out with someone else...

14:27.960 --> 14:29.800
And one day...

14:31.050 --> 14:34.340
He said he loved me more than my boyfriend did.

14:35.220 --> 14:36.850
He said he would die for me.

14:39.440 --> 14:40.440
I couldn't stop him...

14:42.650 --> 14:43.930
He just...

14:46.540 --> 14:48.460
That is why it is my fault.

14:49.390 --> 14:54.730
The busy work, my falling grades, and this leg as well.

14:57.050 --> 15:01.100
In order to become happy, I had to work a lot for it myself, right?

15:03.850 --> 15:07.550
I wonder who has been doing all this.

15:08.280 --> 15:10.830
It's like they are just picking on many schools without reason.

15:11.760 --> 15:13.060
It's not random.

15:13.910 --> 15:16.090
Mostly, there are conditions.

15:16.540 --> 15:18.530
You... don't tell me you looked into it?

15:19.260 --> 15:23.000
I couldn't be sure that you wouldn't be in danger...

15:23.670 --> 15:25.870
so I simply found information.

15:28.470 --> 15:30.720
And? What's the criteria?

15:31.810 --> 15:36.410
I'm just guessing, but maybe it's people who look like they are happy.

15:37.290 --> 15:41.840
Complete happiness probably doesn't matter. Only that the people seem happy to others.

15:42.500 --> 15:44.890
In other words, they look for happiness to destroy.

15:46.780 --> 15:48.780
Just who are these guys?

15:49.270 --> 15:53.470
I don't know, but I did hear several rumors.

15:54.280 --> 15:57.850
There's apparently a mysterious group that works through the Net.

16:11.200 --> 16:12.850
It's just like you guessed.

16:13.580 --> 16:15.830
These guys are certainly becoming more active.

16:16.630 --> 16:19.420
If it goes on like this, someone might get killed.

16:20.150 --> 16:21.020
Agreed.

16:22.380 --> 16:24.730
I will crush these destroyers of happiness.

16:25.990 --> 16:27.960
Will you lend me your power?

16:29.230 --> 16:29.640
Yes.

16:33.240 --> 16:36.840
Mom, it looks like there's enough.

16:37.820 --> 16:39.700
It's about time to gather it all.

16:40.790 --> 16:42.730
So you should look forward to it.

17:01.360 --> 17:03.860
Welcome home, master!

17:10.090 --> 17:11.570
My bust is 84.

17:11.850 --> 17:12.350
Huh?

17:13.030 --> 17:14.630
But you were staring.

17:15.510 --> 17:19.890
By the way, my hips are 83. They are quite good for child bearing!

17:20.080 --> 17:22.090
That's not what I meant by looking!

17:22.430 --> 17:25.760
An appointment, right? Juuzawa Juu.

17:27.020 --> 17:27.560
You--

17:28.400 --> 17:29.810
The person you want to meet...

17:30.800 --> 17:32.390
is there.

17:39.330 --> 17:39.740
Ame!

17:48.270 --> 17:50.780
My name is Kirishima Yukihime.

17:51.400 --> 17:57.430
To make you understand, my family name comes from "I'll slice you before you do, you villain!"

17:57.420 --> 17:58.720
The writing is like this.

17:59.850 --> 18:01.540
Ame!

18:04.320 --> 18:05.410
Endou Madoka.

18:07.170 --> 18:09.530
Juuzawa, do you like virgins?

18:09.910 --> 18:10.160
Huh?

18:10.740 --> 18:14.320
By the way, you know, there are three in this room here.

18:15.090 --> 18:16.190
Now then, who are they?

18:16.760 --> 18:18.050
That's not even a question.

18:18.550 --> 18:26.740
Well, comparing the numbers of times in your life you thought of dying or killing someone, which is greater?

18:27.280 --> 18:28.760
I don't understand the meaning behind that.

18:30.370 --> 18:33.860
You know, I want to know what kind of human you are.

18:34.210 --> 18:37.860
Whether you're a human good for Ame or just trash.

18:38.430 --> 18:39.410
And if I was trash?

18:41.370 --> 18:42.470
What do you think?

18:44.550 --> 18:46.730
That hurt, Madoka! I bit my tongue!

18:46.770 --> 18:48.700
Enough with your messing around.

18:50.910 --> 18:55.550
Sorry about that. For a long time, Yukihime has always gone too far about liking or hating people.

18:57.240 --> 19:01.370
If someone interests her just a little, she tests them many times.

19:02.860 --> 19:06.470
Even though I say that, I don't really like you.

19:07.640 --> 19:10.850
But that doesn't mean it's your fault.

19:11.680 --> 19:13.870
I hate boys and broccoli.

19:15.760 --> 19:17.470
That's how it is. Don't worry about it.

19:19.240 --> 19:20.340
From now on, Juuzawa...

19:21.260 --> 19:22.280
Don't be a molester.

19:22.280 --> 19:23.310
That's--

19:23.310 --> 19:25.460
I SAID I DIDN'T DO IT!

19:25.850 --> 19:28.860
I've been with these two since middle school.

19:29.600 --> 19:35.860
Mostly because we share many memories and interests. However, they are very reliable friends.

19:36.060 --> 19:37.630
So I asked for their aid.

19:39.900 --> 19:40.510
Friends?

19:48.720 --> 19:49.730
Hey, Ame...

19:50.830 --> 19:52.090
What about your clothes?

19:53.980 --> 19:55.340
Is something weird?

19:56.580 --> 19:57.920
No, it's not bad.

20:00.050 --> 20:01.370
Trade-off.

20:04.010 --> 20:08.490
Because Ame asked us for help, she's helping us with this job.

20:09.810 --> 20:14.090
We heard most of the story from Ame. This time it's your turn to talk.

20:14.710 --> 20:15.870
Juuzawa Juu.

20:24.080 --> 20:25.470
Those two were amazing.

20:26.210 --> 20:29.380
By calling just a few phone numbers, they found out where she was staying.

20:29.600 --> 20:30.350
--Absolutely no--

20:31.520 --> 20:33.630
But how are you planning to enter the room?

20:34.500 --> 20:36.600
She's not answering her phone and she may be in there with men.

20:37.180 --> 20:39.340
Moreover, I hear they are a dangerous group.

20:40.110 --> 20:41.310
There's no need to worry.

20:41.780 --> 20:44.460
You should be worried for them instead.

20:55.500 --> 20:56.640
Who are you bastards?!

21:01.480 --> 21:01.970
Don't kill!

21:03.440 --> 21:05.910
Take that guy and disappear right now.

21:08.660 --> 21:12.150
Why? How did you find me? Seriously, impossible.

21:12.460 --> 21:14.400
Does this mean I didn't have enough Happiness?

21:14.850 --> 21:15.680
Happiness?

21:15.860 --> 21:18.060
Even though I went through the trouble of collecting them...

21:18.110 --> 21:19.790
and was looking forward to next week.

21:19.960 --> 21:23.940
I see. Happiness? I understand.

21:24.350 --> 21:24.790
Ame?

21:25.750 --> 21:26.660
Hirose Nao.

21:27.360 --> 21:33.240
Your crime wasn't special. It was revealed because my Happiness is greater than yours.

21:33.300 --> 21:37.930
Huh? How did you do it? Was our way just hopeless?

21:38.440 --> 21:39.480
Do you want to know?

21:39.770 --> 21:40.570
Tell me!

21:41.080 --> 21:45.350
In return, I'll have you tell me everything you know.

21:46.200 --> 21:46.820
Alright?

21:48.120 --> 21:48.510
Yeah.

21:49.420 --> 21:53.370
First, tell us why you targeted Lord Juu.

21:54.210 --> 21:56.020
Oh, I see-- you

21:56.100 --> 21:57.250
Did you forget?!

21:57.560 --> 21:59.670
Because I was only following orders.

22:00.000 --> 22:05.310
If I reported you to the police I'd make a bonus.

22:05.580 --> 22:07.650
Who was the person who gave you those orders?

22:07.980 --> 22:09.190
It was Ms. Kuraki.

22:09.610 --> 22:11.810
She's the leader of our Happiness Club.

22:11.990 --> 22:12.760
Ms. Kuraki.

22:19.390 --> 22:22.810
I never thought a meeting would be at the school.

22:23.090 --> 22:25.930
But why are they holding one all the way out here?

22:26.370 --> 22:29.440
I can't say for sure because I don't have any proof.

22:29.790 --> 22:31.750
I think it would be best to hear it from them.

22:32.900 --> 22:33.930
Here, eh?

22:34.970 --> 22:36.330
These are the original club rooms.

22:36.750 --> 22:39.610
It doesn't look like they have been used in a while though.

22:45.980 --> 22:46.790
Someone is coming out.

22:54.570 --> 22:55.270
Ayase!

22:57.570 --> 22:58.460
Juuzawa!

22:58.680 --> 23:00.050
You-- why--

23:01.250 --> 23:03.560
Don't tell me you're in the Happiness Club?

23:07.570 --> 23:10.410
Even though it's embarrassing to talk about, actually, yes.

23:11.250 --> 23:13.040
But as I thought, I'm scared.

23:13.480 --> 23:16.710
Leave talking for later. We came to crush this club.

23:17.200 --> 23:17.960
Return home.

23:18.590 --> 23:19.810
Thank you, Juuzawa!

23:21.200 --> 23:22.080
Wait, please.

23:22.810 --> 23:24.030
Ayase Ichiko.

23:25.130 --> 23:28.800
You are the leader of the Happiness Club, Kuraki, I assume.

23:32.140 --> 23:34.390
What are you saying, all of a sudden?

23:34.680 --> 23:40.350
Am I wrong? In that case, why did you lock the door when you left?

23:43.210 --> 23:44.210
Ayase! You--

23:46.950 --> 23:50.690
As expected of you, Ochibana. You have a considerable amount of Happiness.

23:50.990 --> 23:51.950
Is that true?

23:53.600 --> 23:58.830
Right. I control all the morons inside there.

23:58.910 --> 24:01.130
The organizer of the Happiness Club.

24:01.520 --> 24:04.420
Why? Why are you doing this?

24:04.560 --> 24:06.730
Because I wanted to become happy!

24:08.630 --> 24:11.710
In what way is all that related to what's going on?!

24:12.050 --> 24:12.980
You don't understand?

24:13.110 --> 24:15.650
True, that is an interesting point of view.

24:16.360 --> 24:22.460
Destroying another person's happiness and then taking it for yourself, correct?

24:23.260 --> 24:29.790
If your premise is that the worlds' total amount of happiness is a constant, then you may be right.

24:30.100 --> 24:33.000
Congratulations. You impress me, Ms. Ochibana.

24:34.230 --> 24:39.490
I only stated the explanation that was the most childish.

24:41.240 --> 24:42.830
Rather harsh.

24:44.610 --> 24:47.510
But, is reality like that, I wonder?

24:49.000 --> 24:55.070
For a person to attain happiness, they will certainly destroy the happiness of another.

24:55.680 --> 24:58.130
Everyone is doing it subconsciously.

24:58.990 --> 25:02.990
I'm only doing it consciously. That's it.

25:04.690 --> 25:07.140
And then I will become happy.

25:07.960 --> 25:09.090
Shocking, eh.

25:09.320 --> 25:11.480
That's a really cynical way to think about it.

25:11.850 --> 25:14.810
Idiotic... really idiotic!

25:15.120 --> 25:16.500
It's your guys' fault!

25:18.540 --> 25:19.350
Hey, Ame--

25:19.770 --> 25:20.270
Guys--

25:20.790 --> 25:21.890
How wonderful.

25:22.170 --> 25:24.520
The "Three Musketeers", I wonder?

25:31.240 --> 25:33.220
Wonder if I should power up...?

25:43.280 --> 25:45.870
Help!

25:54.350 --> 25:58.310
With this, all the happiness they have collected now belongs to me!

26:01.370 --> 26:02.030
Ame!

26:02.070 --> 26:03.050
Yes, Lord Juu!

26:13.020 --> 26:15.760
As I thought, I am the person with the most Happiness.

26:20.230 --> 26:20.940
Juuzawa!

26:23.090 --> 26:24.420
Godamnit!

26:26.950 --> 26:27.800
Lord Juu!

26:34.950 --> 26:36.730
You think she didn't really run away?

26:37.620 --> 26:37.990
Yes.

26:38.620 --> 26:39.550
Why do you think so?

26:40.370 --> 26:43.580
She believes in her own Happiness.

26:44.330 --> 26:45.930
Heh? Why?

26:46.700 --> 26:47.700
I should also be asking why.

26:48.300 --> 26:49.550
I called her.

27:00.120 --> 27:01.360
Sit anywhere.

27:05.770 --> 27:07.570
Lord Juu, take this.

27:08.540 --> 27:10.230
You may need this.

27:15.100 --> 27:17.100
Tea is good, right? Wait a little bit.

27:18.230 --> 27:19.620
You didn't run away?

27:20.570 --> 27:22.390
Why would I need to do that?

27:22.810 --> 27:26.840
With the Happiness I have now, I can avoid elimination.

27:31.860 --> 27:34.720
Just saying, but, calling the police is useless.

27:35.700 --> 27:41.100
I didn't leave anything behind, and I absolutely won't confess.

27:41.750 --> 27:42.750
Even if I die I won't.

27:43.140 --> 27:44.520
What are you saying?

27:44.770 --> 27:47.590
She planned all those incidents.

27:48.460 --> 27:50.590
The group knows her as Kuraki.

27:51.490 --> 27:52.190
There's no mistake.

27:54.050 --> 27:54.920
Kuraki?

27:59.140 --> 28:00.160
Something happen?

28:08.440 --> 28:11.510
I'm called Kuraki because of my father who got divorced.

28:12.050 --> 28:15.340
That's because long ago, Kuraki Ichiko was what I went by.

28:17.880 --> 28:19.990
And my brother's name was... Kuraki Kazuo.

28:23.350 --> 28:27.180
Juuzawa, you heard from Shiraishi, right?

28:28.100 --> 28:30.910
"I've killed someone before."

28:33.230 --> 28:36.080
That is what she does a lot.

28:36.650 --> 28:39.910
Telling people her own secrets of trauma...

28:40.140 --> 28:42.360
she makes them open out their hearts to her.

28:43.680 --> 28:45.560
She's rather good, right?

28:45.920 --> 28:49.110
Up until now, I wonder how many people you've told...

28:49.480 --> 28:50.140
Senior.

28:51.550 --> 28:52.950
And? What about that?

28:53.490 --> 28:55.610
Your mind really is that bad, isn't it?

28:55.920 --> 28:58.270
How many times do I have to explain because you don't understand?

28:58.690 --> 29:01.380
The boy who committed suicide by Shiraishi,

29:02.030 --> 29:03.030
in other words,

29:03.820 --> 29:05.610
is your older brother, right?

29:06.200 --> 29:07.350
That's how it is.

29:08.810 --> 29:10.380
My older brother.

29:11.210 --> 29:13.920
However, the illicit love was a lie.

29:14.650 --> 29:18.070
She was already going out with my older brother.

29:19.610 --> 29:22.030
But one day, he was thrown away all of a sudden.

29:22.670 --> 29:29.920
All for the Student Council President, an heir of a major company, who has excellent grades.

29:32.700 --> 29:35.950
And my despairing brother died.

29:36.810 --> 29:38.580
By slitting his own throat.

29:49.710 --> 29:52.000
Is that true? What she was saying now?

29:54.430 --> 29:56.710
You must hold me in contempt...

29:57.930 --> 29:58.430
No.

30:02.030 --> 30:04.410
Shiraishi, it's not like I hate you.

30:06.420 --> 30:09.870
As a woman, I applaud your calm judgment.

30:11.080 --> 30:15.720
Moreover, I should be grateful to you.

30:16.950 --> 30:17.550
Grateful?

30:18.160 --> 30:23.000
Because you made me realize how this world runs.

30:25.110 --> 30:28.930
The years after my brother's suicide were the worst.

30:29.970 --> 30:33.720
My grandparents died. My father was fired for causing a car accident.

30:34.390 --> 30:37.570
Stress caused my mother to become neurotic, so she stays in bed.

30:39.270 --> 30:42.580
In the end, we lost our home to arson.

30:43.410 --> 30:46.580
My father left my sick mother and went missing.

30:48.390 --> 30:53.820
Even now, my mother isn't able get up from her bed.

30:55.500 --> 30:59.230
Saying it's just bad luck isn't logical.

31:00.380 --> 31:05.090
It seemed like my brother's death caused all our Happiness to go far away.

31:07.660 --> 31:08.980
But what about you?

31:09.420 --> 31:11.830
Shiraishi, you were unfortunate.

31:13.450 --> 31:18.320
The time I entered school here and saw you, I was surprised.

31:19.290 --> 31:23.240
Excellent grades. Popular as the Student Council President.

31:24.180 --> 31:29.050
Even though my older brother was dead, you were blessed with much happiness.

31:30.460 --> 31:32.620
While I was drenched in unhappiness,

31:33.030 --> 31:34.470
you were shining.

31:35.890 --> 31:37.300
I thought...

31:40.580 --> 31:45.540
If was almost as if you took all the happiness from my brother.

31:46.030 --> 31:48.020
That's why you had happiness!

31:49.950 --> 31:52.080
If I apologize-- will it be fine...

31:52.750 --> 31:55.300
It may be true I betrayed Kazuo...

31:56.740 --> 31:58.730
But I didn't think he would have died!

31:59.480 --> 32:01.440
If you want me to apologize, then I'll apologize!

32:01.880 --> 32:02.590
So--

32:03.330 --> 32:04.980
That isn't needed.

32:06.000 --> 32:08.990
It's fine if you just return it.

32:13.960 --> 32:15.370
Mom, I'm coming in.

32:25.470 --> 32:27.520
Ayase! You-- that--

32:28.180 --> 32:29.340
That's my mom.

32:30.230 --> 32:32.280
Just as you see, she's not well.

32:33.040 --> 32:34.580
Seems I made a mistake calculating.

32:35.130 --> 32:37.640
I haven't obtained enough Happiness yet.

32:46.150 --> 32:47.900
No, don't kill me!

32:48.140 --> 32:52.200
Come on, I'm not a murderer!

32:52.860 --> 32:55.220
Just that I only want you to return it.

32:59.220 --> 33:01.800
Give the happiness you took from my brother back.

33:02.230 --> 33:03.730
But how?

33:03.980 --> 33:08.280
It's simple, destroying your happiness will be fine.

33:09.540 --> 33:11.420
For example, you're a beautiful girl.

33:12.180 --> 33:14.860
How does cutting your ears or nose sound?

33:16.110 --> 33:17.510
Eyes would be good.

33:17.950 --> 33:20.740
Ah! Your breasts don't sound bad either!

33:21.340 --> 33:24.830
Come now, please do it yourself.

33:25.400 --> 33:26.640
Forgive me!

33:27.050 --> 33:28.260
Please forgive me!

33:28.760 --> 33:30.690
I'm sorry, forgive me!

33:31.560 --> 33:33.840
Listen up and do it!

33:38.600 --> 33:41.090
If you give back my Happiness,

33:42.050 --> 33:44.070
my mother's illness will be cured.

33:45.360 --> 33:46.980
If I obtain more Happiness,

33:47.310 --> 33:48.880
my father might even come back!

33:49.310 --> 33:52.500
Perhaps my big brother may be able to return!

33:53.000 --> 33:53.970
So... okay?

33:55.120 --> 33:56.450
No! Forgive me!

33:56.510 --> 33:58.230
Hey, where should I do it?

33:58.880 --> 33:59.990
It's alright.

34:00.140 --> 34:00.980
-Your ears?

34:01.030 --> 34:06.590
The ordinary and the abnormal are similar but the distinction is how you look at it.

34:06.600 --> 34:09.590
- Maybe I should cut some meat from your face!

34:07.600 --> 34:09.220
It's alright, Lord Juu.

34:09.690 --> 34:11.970
You won't lose to something like this.

34:12.640 --> 34:14.080
Your fingers would be good!

34:15.290 --> 34:16.510
But be careful, okay?

34:17.030 --> 34:19.440
If you die, it would be troublesome to get rid of your corpse...

34:19.960 --> 34:21.780
so please take caution, okay?

34:22.860 --> 34:24.850
Lord Juu, I have a request.

34:25.420 --> 34:27.700
Please give your orders to me.

34:28.300 --> 34:29.070
End it.

34:29.540 --> 34:29.930
Your will.

34:30.770 --> 34:33.960
I will deal judgment upon these unsightly people.

34:34.130 --> 34:35.960
I'm telling you to do it!

34:35.940 --> 34:36.940
Forgive me!

34:38.470 --> 34:40.530
Ayase, I would like to talk.

34:40.740 --> 34:42.200
Can't you leave it until later?

34:42.280 --> 34:43.780
This is an important time.

34:44.330 --> 34:47.430
However, there is one thing that is bothering me.

34:48.170 --> 34:49.100
Shiraishi.

34:51.130 --> 34:55.830
Ayase's older brother committed suicide right before your eyes, right?

34:58.340 --> 34:59.030
Yes...

34:59.470 --> 35:02.650
He was ready to die for your sake, then he really died.

35:03.490 --> 35:06.720
At that time, what kind of expression did he have?

35:11.350 --> 35:12.080
He smiled...

35:12.660 --> 35:13.550
Did he look happy?

35:14.050 --> 35:16.100
Yes... he was smiling happily...

35:16.520 --> 35:19.810
I don't even know why, but he was smiling!

35:21.100 --> 35:23.780
Ochibana, just what are you saying?

35:24.440 --> 35:30.660
Ayase, your family's Happiness was not taken by Shiraishi.

35:31.540 --> 35:36.290
That can't be, because when my brother died--

35:36.630 --> 35:37.720
Did you realize?

35:40.120 --> 35:44.270
Your family's Happiness was snatched away by your older brother.

35:45.050 --> 35:48.690
His own death destroyed your family's happiness.

35:49.270 --> 35:51.840
With that, he took that happiness.

35:53.770 --> 35:58.060
And, he had the most happiness in his life before he died. It was eternal.

35:58.910 --> 36:00.580
It was eternal.

36:01.830 --> 36:07.370
He wished to take his family's happiness for himself, and did so magnificently.

36:09.400 --> 36:13.440
You're saying he knew that would happen if he died? That's not true!!

36:13.680 --> 36:15.740
It's not about whether he knew or not.

36:18.290 --> 36:24.040
For people to become happy, they will without fail destroy another's happiness.

36:25.940 --> 36:29.010
This is what you said before, Ayase.

36:38.470 --> 36:40.620
You're cruel... big brother...

36:49.790 --> 36:51.200
Destroying Happiness, huh...?

36:52.590 --> 36:56.440
Doing something like that... was she really happy?

36:57.380 --> 36:58.450
I think so.

36:58.930 --> 37:04.180
By believing in what she was doing, she thought her hard times would end.

37:05.220 --> 37:08.680
Isn't that only turning your eyes away from reality?

37:09.300 --> 37:10.060
That is so.

37:10.800 --> 37:15.640
The efficient way to become happy is to not look at reality.

37:18.110 --> 37:20.100
What does happiness mean to you?

37:24.960 --> 37:28.570
It is the feeling I have right now.

37:30.320 --> 37:34.980
Umm, Ame, there's something I need to tell you.

37:36.220 --> 37:36.590
Yes?

37:38.440 --> 37:41.740
It's about the "lover" that saved me from the molester incident...

37:42.620 --> 37:44.230
That's not what you told me!

37:44.450 --> 37:48.100
I told you she was the only person you shouldn't tell, why did you have to?!

37:48.180 --> 37:48.850
Hikaru?

37:49.000 --> 37:49.600
Yes!

37:50.700 --> 37:51.870
Listen to my story.

37:54.360 --> 37:56.200
I was very happy.

37:57.110 --> 38:01.800
You saved Lord Juu from an incident I didn't know about.

38:02.800 --> 38:03.390
That's it.

38:05.030 --> 38:07.950
To return the favor, I cleared the misunderstanding.

38:09.490 --> 38:10.530
With that Ibuki guy.

38:12.670 --> 38:15.880
Go to him. He'll listen to you properly now.

38:16.680 --> 38:17.840
But-- how?

38:17.970 --> 38:23.000
You know, Juuzawa had a one-to-one duel for your sake.

38:23.860 --> 38:27.810
He stood there without landing one shot until Ibuki gave up beating him up.

38:29.520 --> 38:33.180
Boys can do amazing things sometimes, right?

38:34.140 --> 38:35.240
Why would you go that far?

38:36.190 --> 38:37.990
You helped me too, right?

38:39.140 --> 38:40.290
That's the only reason?

38:41.160 --> 38:41.400
Yeah.

38:42.910 --> 38:44.800
Don't mislead me, idiot!

38:45.280 --> 38:47.630
You made me think of something weird!

38:50.620 --> 38:52.470
You should go and be with her.

38:53.430 --> 38:54.200
Because you're the older sister.

38:55.020 --> 38:55.590
However--

38:56.450 --> 39:00.870
If it goes well, give her your blessing, for her happiness.

39:03.520 --> 39:03.880
Yes!

39:24.620 --> 39:25.490
Juuzawa.

39:27.840 --> 39:28.990
Shiraishi!

39:30.080 --> 39:31.520
Did you have a childhood dream?

39:32.480 --> 39:38.380
You know, I wanted to become happy.

39:40.290 --> 39:43.260
For that sake, I've always worked hard to get there.

39:44.460 --> 39:46.850
Everyone who was in my way was eliminated.

39:48.490 --> 39:51.290
Kazuo too...

39:54.380 --> 39:56.040
And it was going so well.

39:57.740 --> 39:59.510
Even though it was all going well...

40:00.990 --> 40:02.200
It's the end already.

40:03.320 --> 40:05.040
My happiness is no longer...

40:05.360 --> 40:06.200
What do you mean?

40:07.040 --> 40:11.220
Hey, Juuzawa, you--

40:13.120 --> 40:14.910
I have one request of you.

40:15.980 --> 40:16.610
Give it...

40:20.680 --> 40:22.230
Give it to me.

40:23.050 --> 40:23.850
I see--

40:23.940 --> 40:25.400
Give me your Happiness.

40:26.980 --> 40:28.980
You also destroy Happiness.

40:33.870 --> 40:34.720
Ame?

40:39.990 --> 40:41.220
It was a car accident.

40:41.540 --> 40:43.640
A high school student was hit.

40:44.930 --> 40:45.770
Lord Juu!

40:47.460 --> 40:49.400
Lord Juu! Lord Juu!!

40:51.590 --> 40:52.630
Lord Juu--

40:53.800 --> 40:54.300
Ame...

40:55.600 --> 40:57.020
Lord Juu...

41:08.330 --> 41:12.160
Not many people still believe in karma or cause and effect.

41:12.900 --> 41:15.140
Because this world is a lazy being.

41:16.350 --> 41:18.700
But once in a while, it does a good job.

41:23.950 --> 41:27.890
You... you do well knowing when I'm in danger.

41:33.090 --> 41:35.550
It's our bond from our past lives.

41:35.550 --> 41:40.180
Kanojo

41:40.540 --> 41:45.420
I was alone; that time was always like that.

41:46.000 --> 41:49.860
I wanted to erase myself.

41:51.890 --> 42:03.200
A place where I didn't belong, the corner of the classroom.

42:03.200 --> 42:09.580
Frustrated; Scared.

42:09.780 --> 42:14.540
I wanted to close this door.

42:14.850 --> 42:24.850
Someday, if I could have the courage to talk to you.

42:25.180 --> 42:28.130
Just--

42:28.550 --> 42:34.180
If living hurts this much...

42:34.250 --> 42:39.250
If it would give you happiness.

42:39.490 --> 42:48.800
I didn't realize, thank you for telling me.

42:48.990 --> 42:51.600
I understand now.

42:51.800 --> 43:00.210
I knew pain and great kindness.

43:00.430 --> 43:10.020
I believe in myself to keep on walking, so I can break away from my past.

43:10.040 --> 43:17.110
My future depends on myself.

43:19.180 --> 43:22.350
Just--

43:22.410 --> 43:33.420
If living has so much meaning...

43:33.620 --> 43:42.470
then I can do it and I won't lose to tomorrow.

43:42.670 --> 43:47.250
Someday I'll smile and tell you:

43:47.400 --> 44:00.000
"I realized that living is an important thing."
